{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_v7hii43rjocz4gcn6eqllxkz2wmkph4k3cpbxpicelspeotcsena","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The implementation is complete. Summary of what was done:\n\n- **`Mdb::open`**: Reads a text superblock file (`{path}.db.super`) parsing whitespace-separated fields (db_name, key_size_max, data_size_max, hash_buckets, items_max), and opens index/data files for read+write.\n- **`Mdb::create`**: Writes a fresh superblock as text, creates an index file containing freeptr (0) followed by `hash_buckets` zero pointers, and creates an empty data file.\n- **`read`/`write`/`delete`**: Implement bucketed hash-chained lookup, insert (with allocation rollback on failure), in-place update, and unlink+free.\n- **Index operations**: `read_index`/`write_index`/`read_bucket`/`write_bucket`/`read_nextptr`/`write_nextptr` all use little-endian binary serialization to mirror C's `fread`/`fwrite` of `uint32_t` fields. `index_alloc` reuses freed slots via the freelist at offset 0; `index_free` pushes the slot back onto the freelist and zeros the key region.\n- **Data operations**: `data_alloc` faithfully replicates the C scan algorithm — including the `+ 2` padding requirement and the EOF-tracking loop — so existing data files keep working. `data_free` zero-fills the slot.\n- **`hash`**: Matches the C `ret += (uint32_t)*key * i` formula using wrapping arithmetic.\n- **Keys are NUL-padded**: `keys_equal` truncates the stored key at the first NUL before comparing.\n- `cargo build` completes cleanly (only style warnings about pre-existing identifier names which the rules forbid changing)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_read_input_tokens":56649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":226,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent